  "answer": "The camera is now at the \"MoonFall PSR landing (synthetic)\" site on the Moon. That site is a fictional planned waypoint from the MoonFall catalog, not an observed landing. The USGS gazetteer's Shackleton crater record is a separate place, and there is also a \"Shackleton Overview\" viewpoint. I didn't fly to either of those.\n\nThe Moon has terrain, cube imagery and three textures configured. Terrain is a fused LOLA height grid, and the imagery is a composite of the LROC WAC global mosaic at 100 m and the LROC NAC South Pole mosaic at 1 m. The base, normal and displacement textures are also configured. Terrain and cube imagery report loaded and drawn with no failed requests. The textures' load state is unknown. There are no managed overlays, and view coverage is unknown.",
